INT. PAWNSHOP BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Shelves of guitars, clocks, and cameras. A caged bulb. A safe, door ajar.

ROSALIND "ROZ" VANTERPOOL, 40s, in a trench coat, holds a gun on VINCENT "VINNIE" OKAFOR, 50s, behind a desk. He raises both hands, a cigar still smoldering between his fingers.

ROZ
Open it.

VINNIE
It's open.

ROZ
All the way.

VINNIE
It's a good safe. It doesn't go all the way.

ROZ
Vinnie.

VINNIE ^
Roz.

They speak together, then both stop. Roz tightens her grip. Vinnie ashes the cigar on the desk.

VINNIE (CONT'D)
You hired me, remember?

ROZ
I remember.

She steps forward and slams the safe door wide. Inside: a single sheet of paper. She grabs it. He grabs her wrist. They struggle, knocking a lamp off the desk. The bulb swings. The gun goes off, shattering a clock.

They freeze.

ROZ (CONT'D)
(reading)
This is a receipt.

VINNIE
For what you paid me.

ROZ
That's all there is?

VINNIE
That's all there ever was.

She lowers the gun. The clock keeps ticking, in pieces.
